    "narrative": "The daily optimizer identifies **Mickey Moniak** as our premier play, boasting an elite score of 75.98. His start against Roki Sasaki is bolstered by a favorable 14% park adjustment and a significant 14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage. Furthermore, the 2% efficiency bump from the opponent's slow delivery\u2014an often-overlooked variable for our SB-focused strategy\u2014cements his position as a must-start. **Jose Caballero** also surges into elite territory with a 64.59 score, largely due to a massive 19% boost from opposing pitcher Chris Bassitt\u2019s profile, which overrides the inherent penalty of batting in the nine-hole. **Isaac Paredes** rounds out our top-tier recommendations at 64.31, capitalizing on a strong platoon matchup against Walbert Ure\u00f1a to provide stable production.\n\nWhile the roster remains aggressive, the tightest decision occurred at the fringe of our starting nine, where **Austin Riley** (54.15) was narrowly edged out by the superior efficiency profile of **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Max Muncy**. Despite **Austin Riley** benefiting from a slight boost due to his ability to exploit slow pitching deliveries, his position low in the batting order proved to be a net negative compared to the middle-of-the-order security offered by our starters. Meanwhile, **Zach McKinstry** remains firmly benched with a 34.56 score, falling well below our 40-point efficiency floor due to a brutal matchup against the arm of Paul Skenes, which triggered a 19% downgrade for SP skill.\n\nRisk management remains a primary focus today, as most of our core, including **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Max Muncy**, **Cole Young**, **Brice Turang**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Griffin Conine**, are operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status. While we have projected their batting positions, any late-scratch or order-shuffle could volatility impact these scores. Notably, **Corbin Carroll** faces a difficult task against Payton Tolle; despite his elite speed, the combination of a tough left-handed matchup and a 14% negative adjustment for the starter's skill profile keeps his score at a modest 56.41. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood**, who remains on the IL and unavailable for any potential rotation.",
